Question 7:The Faulty  Manipal Weather Station

AIM: Handling missing values, dropping faulty rows, and comparing mean vs median for robustness.

Code:
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

weather = pd.DataFrame({
    'day': range(1, 11),
    'temp_c': [28.1, 29.0, np.nan, 30.2, 29.5, 55.0, np.nan, 27.8, 28.6, 29.3],
    'humidity': [64, 61, 63, np.nan, 60, 58, np.nan, 66, 65, 62]
})
print("Missing per column:\n", weather.isna().sum())
print("\nRows with any missing:", weather.isna().any(axis=1).sum())
weather = weather.dropna(subset=['temp_c','humidity'], how='all')
print("\nRows after dropping:", len(weather))
weather['temp_c'].fillna(weather['temp_c'].median(), inplace=True)
weather['humidity'].fillna(weather['humidity'].median(), inplace=True)
print("\nTemperature mean:", round(weather['temp_c'].mean(),2))
print("Temperature median:", round(weather['temp_c'].median(),2))

Output:
